Subject: [PATCH 0020] Describe the decoder buffer at its visible height

The decoder hands out 1920x1088 buffers for 1080p, and the stream window
described that padded height to the compositor. Weston then refused the buffer
as larger than the configured fullscreen state and raised a protocol error,
which kills the whole Wayland connection: the first frame took the application
down with it.

The plane offsets already describe where the chroma rows live, so the padding
never has to be mentioned. Describe the buffer at the visible height and the
surface matches the fullscreen configuration exactly.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [STM32MP25 performance work]

diff --git a/native/opennow-streamer/crates/opennow-streamer-platform-linux/src/frame_producer.rs b/native/opennow-streamer/crates/opennow-streamer-platform-linux/src/frame_producer.rs
index d609650e..1a412a38 100644
--- a/native/opennow-streamer/crates/opennow-streamer-platform-linux/src/frame_producer.rs
+++ b/native/opennow-streamer/crates/opennow-streamer-platform-linux/src/frame_producer.rs
@@ -466,16 +466,16 @@ fn export_dmabuf(frame: &DecodedVideoFrame) -> Option<DmabufExport> {
     if fd < 0 {
         return None;
     }
-    let height = match layer.planes.len() {
-        2 => crate::format::nv12_coded_height(&layer.planes[0], &layer.planes[1], frame.format.height),
-        _ => frame.format.height,
-    };
+    // The buffer is described at the visible height even when the decoder pads
+    // the picture (1088 rows for 1080p): the planes carry their own offsets, so
+    // the extra rows never reach the compositor, and a surface matching the
+    // fullscreen size is the only kind the compositor accepts.
     let mut export = DmabufExport {
         fd,
         format: layer.format,
         modifier: object.format_modifier,
         width: frame.format.width,
-        height,
+        height: frame.format.height,
         plane_count: layer.planes.len() as u32,
         ..DmabufExport::default()
     };
